From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:01:12 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 01/48] net: xpon: omci: wrap the MIB data sync counter from
 255 to 1

G.988 (ONU data, MIB data sync; MIB synchronisation annex) reserves the
value 0 for the state right after a MIB reset or instantiation. Every
successful Create, Delete and Set from the OLT moves the counter on, and
it wraps from 255 to 1. The OLT keeps the same sequence and audits it
against the ONU data ME.

The agent incremented a u8 and so went from 255 to 0. After 256 changes
since the last MIB reset the ONU reported "just reset" and from then on
stayed one behind the OLT on every wrap, which a MIB audit treats as a
lost MIB and answers with a MIB reset and a full re-provisioning.

MIB data sync is also writable. A Set of it stored the value and then
counted the Set on top, so what the OLT wrote never read back. Keep the
written value instead of incrementing in that case.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 net/xpon/omci/agent.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++--
 net/xpon/omci/me.h    |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/xpon/omci/agent.c b/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
index 708c896..7acc45d 100644
--- a/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
+++ b/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
@@ -703,9 +703,16 @@ static void omci_agent_set_mib_sync_locked(struct omci_agent *agent, u8 sync)
 		object->data[0] = sync;
 }
 
+/*
+ * G.988 ONU data, MIB data sync: 0 only follows a MIB reset; each
+ * successful Create, Delete and Set the OLT sends moves it on, from 255
+ * to 1, never back to 0.
+ */
 static void omci_agent_increment_mib_sync_locked(struct omci_agent *agent)
 {
-	omci_agent_set_mib_sync_locked(agent, (u8)(agent->mib_sync + 1));
+	u8 sync = agent->mib_sync + 1;
+
+	omci_agent_set_mib_sync_locked(agent, sync ? sync : 1);
 }
 
 static int omci_mib_store_locked(struct omci_agent *agent,
@@ -3935,7 +3942,15 @@ static u8 omci_agent_set_locked(struct omci_device *odev, u16 class_id,
 		if (ret)
 			goto rollback_processing;
 	}
-	omci_agent_increment_mib_sync_locked(agent);
+	/*
+	 * MIB data sync is writable: the OLT aligns its copy by setting it,
+	 * so keep the value it wrote instead of counting the Set on top.
+	 */
+	if (class_id == OMCI_CLASS_ONU_DATA && !entity_id &&
+	    (mask & OMCI_ONU_DATA_MIB_SYNC_MASK))
+		omci_agent_set_mib_sync_locked(agent, object->data[0]);
+	else
+		omci_agent_increment_mib_sync_locked(agent);
 	ret = OMCI_RESULT_SUCCESS;
 	goto out_free_previous;
 
diff --git a/net/xpon/omci/me.h b/net/xpon/omci/me.h
index 11ae49b..ca150a6 100644
--- a/net/xpon/omci/me.h
+++ b/net/xpon/omci/me.h
@@ -11,6 +11,8 @@ struct omci_me_class;
 struct omci_mib_object;
 
 #define OMCI_CLASS_ONU_DATA		2
+/* ONU data attribute 1, MIB data sync */
+#define OMCI_ONU_DATA_MIB_SYNC_MASK	BIT(15)
 #define OMCI_CLASS_CARDHOLDER		5
 #define OMCI_CLASS_CIRCUIT_PACK		6
 #define OMCI_CLASS_SOFTWARE_IMAGE	7
